---
description: Keep files and functions within sane size limits; extract before they sprawl.
alwaysApply: false
---

# Size limits

- Files: aim under ~400 lines, hard ceiling ~1000. Past the soft limit, extract cohesive modules rather than appending.
- Functions: aim under ~50 lines. Extract helpers when a function grows past one screen or mixes concerns.
- A `switch`/`match` over a typed union that grows past ~10 cases: extract each case body to a sibling file and call it from the case. Keep the switch. Do not convert it to a registry or lookup table as part of a size fix — that is a behavior-changing refactor.
- Pre-existing large files are grandfathered — don't rewrite them wholesale to satisfy this rule; split when you're already changing them.
